        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I wrote the answer to `answer.json`: `Bbox.from_bounds` receives **left = 0.98, bottom = 0.95, width = 0.0, height = 0.0**.\n\nThis comes from what I know of how `Legend.set_bbox_to_anchor` usually works, not from checking this repository. I didn't open the test file or the matplotlib source here; I only read the question file. In standard matplotlib, when the method gets a 2-tuple `(x, y)`, it becomes `[x, y, 0, 0]`: the two values are kept as the corner position and width and height are set to zero. That's then passed to `Bbox.from_bounds`. So `(0.98, 0.95)` becomes `(0.98, 0.95, 0, 0)`.\n\nIf this copy of matplotlib handles 2-element bboxes differently, or the test's first call uses other values, the answer would be wrong. Reading the method's source and the test's `ax.legend(...)` call would settle it.",
